          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The <strong class="text-white">best harness for zipline riding</strong> is the one certified for the load case you are actually creating. For an adult riding repeatedly, that is the <strong class="text-white">Petzl AVAO SIT FAST</strong> with its EN 813 suspension rating, or the <strong class="text-white">Petzl FALCON</strong> if hanging comfort on long rides matters most. For a child under 30 kg, it is a full-body harness — the <strong class="text-white">Petzl SIMBA</strong> or <strong class="text-white">Edelrid Fraggle III</strong> — and nothing else. Where inversion is possible, step up to a full-body or a sit-plus-chest combination.
